--- comment that would be posted ---
**Validated — deploy-ready.**

I exercised the fix against a throwaway build of `main` (9461bc30b), driving the real rule path: demo-demo case with an active insulin infusion at 2 units/hr, then an eGFR observation followed by a glucose observation to raise `GLUCOSE_UPDATED`.

- **Positive:** with eGFR `>90`, `<15`, and a result-less (null) eGFR row — the exact Sentry condition — the rule evaluated to `true` each time and the alert landed in `rule_fired_results`. It also reads back through the clinician-facing alert API ("Change Insulin Infusion Rate to 6.8 Units/hr"). Ten clean firings, zero rule errors.
- **Negative:** for every unreadable eGFR the calculation text carries no "ISC has been adjusted for eGFR" clause, and nothing was written to `rule_failure_results`. With DIABETES_TYPE_1 on the patient it correctly shows the Type 1 clause alone.
- **Red check:** I compiled the pre-fix class into the running container and re-sent the same input — it reproduced the reported NPE at `generateExpandedCalculation`, recorded a rule failure and produced no alert. Restoring the shipped class (md5 verified) made the same input fire cleanly again. I also flipped the eGFR to a numeric `30` to confirm the clause I assert absent can actually appear, then reverted it.

One thing to keep in mind: `<15` is genuinely below the 45 threshold but is still discarded. That is intended here and tracked in OR-2744.

Existing unit coverage in `AdjustInsulinInfusionRateRuleTest` is solid. I will add the missing Type 1 + numeric eGFR combined-clause case, a service-level test for the initial ISC with an unreadable eGFR, and a supplemental qa-suite end-to-end regression.

Implementation: [PR #4312](https://github.com/guidedclinical/orci/pull/4312)
Validated against `9461bc30bba0a293a6af847f4dd9bcb92054f292` in an isolated ephemeral environment.
